      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Braids (e.g., see figure 1b) are close relatives of knots and links. Berger\n(1991) shows how to define a third order winding number for braids on three\nstrings. It is exactly the third order linking number for those braids cor-\nresponding to three component links with Ly2 = L23 = L3; = 0. A braid\non three strings is specified by three curves 2;(é) (¢ = 1,2,3) in the com-\nplex plane C. The planes of constant ¢ are cross-sections of the braid, which\nstretches from ¢ = 0 to t = 1. It is sometimes helpful to visualise the braid\nas a single curve in C® by writing y(t) = (21(¢), 22(t), 23(¢)). Links",
